The firmament is the shell around [[Færrin]]. Before it cracked the world was mundane: no magic in the air, and no worlds in the night sky. A crack opened in it before 0ag, and magic flooded through; the [[Iridescent Host]] later spoke through the same crack, which shows in the day sky as a second sun. The [[Pharos]] is said to reach it, and the dead pass through the tower to the [[Geography/Godhome|Godhome]] beyond.

Under [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/index|Hallia]], in the straight hall beneath [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Teller's Run/index|Teller's Run]], there is a hairline crack in the air like a fracture in a clear pane of glass. It gives off a concentration of magic too great to measure and will not open. The Party takes it for a smaller version of the crack in the firmament, and for what the pumps nearby are gathering magic to widen. Those pumps have stopped, their control system destroyed in the explosion beneath [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Teller's Run/index|Teller's Run]].
